    "result_text": "All 60 tests pass. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved the date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July), building on the fact that the owner's `registrationDate` is already stored business-day-adjusted at creation time.\n\n**OpenAPI spec** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`):\n- Added a new read-only `fiscalYear` property to the `OwnerDto` schema (format `FY<YY>`, example `FY26`), so the generated DTO gains a `setFiscalYear`.\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` description \u2014 its `-M<YY>` segment now uses the fiscal year rather than the calendar year.\n- Updated the `membershipPoints` description \u2014 tenure is now \"at least one elapsed fiscal year\" instead of \"more than 365 days\".\n\n**Mapper** (`OwnerMapper.java`):\n- Added `@Mapping(target = \"fiscalYear\", ...)` and a `fiscalYear(Owner)` method returning `FY<YY>`.\n- Added a shared `fiscalYearStart(LocalDate)` helper: the fiscal year starts 1 July, so dates in Jul\u2013Dec map to their own calendar year and Jan\u2013Jun map to the prior year.\n- `membershipNumber` now derives its `<YY>` from `fiscalYearStart(registrationDate)` (keeps it consistent with `fiscalYear`, as `Cp14Tests` asserts).\n- Tenure in `membershipPoints` now counts elapsed fiscal years (`fiscalYearStart(now) - fiscalYearStart(registrationDate) >= 1`) instead of a 365-day window; a newly created owner still has zero elapsed fiscal years, so the tenure bonus and the level-4 cap behavior (`Cp39`, `Cp40`) are preserved.\n\n### Notes on the interpretation I chose\n- **Naming convention:** `FY<YY>` uses the *starting* calendar year of the fiscal year (a date of 2026-08-11 \u2192 `FY26`). This keeps the pre-existing `membershipNumber` example (`SMI-0007-M26`) valid. No test pins a specific FY value, so this is a judgment call.\n- **Tenure threshold:** the spec said to count tenure \"in elapsed fiscal years rather than 365-day windows\" but didn't restate the exact cutoff. I used `>= 1` elapsed fiscal year (crossing at least one 1-July boundary), which most closely preserves the old \"~a year of membership earns the bonus\" behavior. No test exercises a positive-tenure owner, so this is the only unverified-by-test piece \u2014 flagging it in case a stricter cutoff (`> 1`) was intended.",
